---
description: SQLAlchemy standards
alwaysApply: true
---

Use:
- SQLAlchemy 2.x style (`Mapped`, `mapped_column`)
- `AsyncSession` / `async_sessionmaker`
- Explicit transactions in the adapter
- A repository class that implements a domain port

Prefer:
- Session factory injected into the repository constructor
- Table classes named `*Table`, distinct from domain entities

Avoid:
- A "service layer" on top of use cases — application use cases are the orchestration
- Raw SQL when ORM is sufficient
- N+1 queries
- Importing SQLAlchemy from `domain`, `application`, or `interfaces`
